# Markdown tables — aligned pipes

When writing Markdown tables, pad cell contents with spaces so every `|` in a column lines up vertically. Do this in plans, READMEs, reports, and any agent-authored Markdown.

## Required form

```markdown
| Field         | Type   | Description        |
|---------------|--------|--------------------|
| `description` | string | What the rule does |
| `globs`       | string | File pattern       |
| `alwaysApply` | boolean| Applies every turn |
```

## Forbidden form

```markdown
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `description` | string | What the rule does |
| `globs` | string | File pattern |
```

## Rules

- Compute column widths from the widest cell in each column (including header).
- Pad cells on the right with spaces so separators share a vertical column.
- Keep the separator row (`---`) the same width as its column.
- Prefer left-aligned text; use leading spaces only when intentionally centering/right-aligning.
- Never emit cramped tables where `|` positions jump between rows.
